  "Question": "The graph of the linear function \\(y=kx+b\\) passes through \\((1,2)\\) and \\((3,-2)\\). The solution set of the inequality \\(kx+b>0\\) is \\(x<a\\). Find the value of \\(a\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "2",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The two points give \\(k=-2\\) and \\(b=4\\), so \\(y=-2x+4\\). Setting \\(y=0\\) gives \\(x=2\\). Since \\(k<0\\), when \\(y>0\\), \\(x<2\\), so \\(a=2\\).",
